{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>To the land of Canaan</b> — like \"and the prophecy of Oded the prophet\" (II Chronicles 15:8), and the sense is: to the land, the land of Canaan — the language of Rabbi Abraham (Ibn Ezra on Numbers 34:2). And so Rashi wrote (Genesis 31:13). And they brought for comparison \"El Bethel,\" and I have already explained its secret (there). But what seems correct in my eyes regarding <b>to the land of Canaan</b> is that the name of this land is Canaan, just as Egypt is the name of the land identical to the name of the people, and likewise \"inhabitants of Canaan\" (Exodus 15:15), and likewise \"Canaan, land of the Philistines, and I will destroy you so that there is no inhabitant\" (Zephaniah 2:5). And so \"to the land of Canaan\" is like saying \"the city Jerusalem\" and \"King David\" (I Kings 1:1) and \"the man Gabriel\" (Daniel 9:21)."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:10:19.235131613Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}